            <blockquote>For watermark purposes, the IP address and device time zone are read at render time only, used to compose the watermark text, and are not written to the database, written to application logs, or sent to any third party. Rate limiting is handled differently; see Section 5.</blockquote>
            <h3>Involving only the site owner</h3>
            <p>The admin panel uses Supabase authentication, and only the site owner has an account. Passwords are stored as one-way hashes. Visitors need no account and no login to read or comment.</p>

            <h2 id="use">2. How each item is used</h2>
            <div class="table-wrap"><table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Data</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Used for anything else?</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Display name</td><td>Displayed publicly alongside the comment</td><td>No</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Email address</td><td>Identifying the commenter; contacting the commenter in the event of a dispute</td><td><strong>Not displayed publicly, not used for marketing, not provided to third parties, not sold</strong></td></tr>
                <tr><td>Comment text</td><td>Displayed publicly under the relevant post once approved</td><td>No</td></tr>
                <tr><td>IP address</td><td>Generating the provenance watermark; rate limiting for unlock attempts and certain endpoints (see Section 5)</td><td>Not used for profiling; no access history retained by this site</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Time zone</td><td><strong>Solely</strong> to compute the local date shown on the watermark</td><td>Same as above</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table></div>
            <p>This site does not carry out user profiling, behavioural analysis, interest tagging, personalised recommendations, advertising, or data trading.</p>

            <h2 id="watermark">3. About the page watermark</h2>
            <p>Pages on this site carry a low-opacity overlay of diagonal text, serving as a provenance mark.</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Composition</strong>: <code>IP label · visitor's local date · site name</code>
                <ul>
                  <li>IPv4 addresses are shown in full; IPv6 addresses are truncated to the first four segments (e.g. <code>240e:39e:490:b5b1</code>) to limit length</li>
                </ul>
              </li>
              <li><strong>Purpose</strong>: to identify the source of leakage where content is reproduced in full or screenshots circulate; a minimal protective measure for original content.</li>
              <li><strong>Limits of processing</strong>: no browsing history is recorded, no personal profile is created, the label is not linked to other access data, and it is not provided to third parties (analytics services are addressed separately in Section 6).</li>
              <li><strong>Visibility</strong>: opacity is low, so it is not readily apparent during normal reading and does not interfere with clicking or text selection.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Visitors who prefer not to see the watermark may hide the element with a browser extension or browse in private mode. No functionality depends on the watermark, and hiding it does not affect access to content.</p>

            <h2 id="cookies">4. Cookies and local storage</h2>
            <p>This site uses no advertising cookies and does not carry out cross-site tracking. Cookies fall into two categories: those necessary for site functionality, which require no consent, and those set only after the visitor has consented (Google Analytics).</p>
            <div class="table-wrap"><table class="table-wide">
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th><th>Consent required</th></tr>
