            <h2 id="thirdparty">5. Third-party services involved</h2>
            <p>This site does not operate its own server; all requests are handled through the third-party services listed below. In addition, rate limiting for unlock attempts on protected posts, and for the translation and excerpt endpoints, writes visitors' IP addresses to the site database, as described at the end of this section.</p>
            <div class="table-wrap"><table>
              <thead>
                <tr><th>Service</th><th>Role</th><th>Data involved</th></tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosting, global content delivery, <strong>Web Analytics</strong></td><td>Request routing; analytics uses no cookies and no device fingerprinting (the platform handles network-level logs under its own policies)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Database, authentication, and object storage</td><td>Posts, comments (including display name, email, and deletion token), site owner account, and rate-limiting records (including IP addresses)</td></tr>
                <tr><td>GitHub</td><td>Code hosting</td><td>No visitor data</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Zhipu GLM (bigmodel.cn)</td><td>Language model service used by the site owner when drafting and translating posts</td><td>Processes only text submitted by the site owner; no visitor data</td></tr>
