              </tbody>
            </table></div>
            <p>This site does not use Baidu Analytics, Umeng, 51LA or other Chinese analytics platforms, and carries no advertising networks, affiliate marketing, or behavioural tracking scripts.</p>
            <h3>Temporary storage of IP addresses</h3>
            <p>To prevent brute-force attempts and endpoint abuse, the following operations write the visitor's IP address to the site database:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Unlocking a protected post</strong>: keyed as <code>rl:unlock:ip:&lt;IP address&gt;</code>, recording request counts and failure counts in order to limit attempt frequency and impose a temporary lock after repeated failures;</li>
              <li><strong>Translation and excerpt endpoints</strong>: counted per account identifier; no separate IP record is kept.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Unlock-related records are held in the <code>rate_limit_state</code> and <code>unlock_fail_state</code> tables, keyed by plaintext IP address, for the purpose of rolling counting windows. Such records are not linked to comments, email addresses, or other identity information, are not used for profiling, and are retained as described in Section 7.</p>

            <h2 id="analytics">6. Analytics and visitors' choices</h2>
            <p>Analytics on this site is used solely to understand traffic and the engagement and retention of content: which posts are actually read, where visitors come from, whether they move on to other posts, and whether they return. Such information is used only to determine content direction and improvements, and for no other purpose.</p>
            <p>Two analytics services are in use. They differ in nature and should be understood separately.</p>
            <h3>1. Cloudflare Web Analytics (always enabled, no consent required)</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>No cookies, no local storage, no device fingerprinting.</li>
              <li>Records aggregated page-level metrics only: page views, referrers, country or region, and page performance.</li>
              <li>According to Cloudflare, Web Analytics does not collect or use visitors' personal data and does not use cookies or device fingerprinting for analytics. It operates independently of the optional Google Analytics service, and this site provides no separate switch for it.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>2. Google Analytics (not loaded by default; consent required)</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>On the first visit, a notice appears at the bottom of the page asking whether Google Analytics may be loaded.</li>
              <li>Neither option is preselected, and both buttons are equally prominent.</li>
              <li>Before the visitor clicks "Accept", the Google Analytics script is neither downloaded nor requested; it is not a case of loading first and blocking reporting afterwards.</li>
              <li>If the visitor declines, Google Analytics is never loaded and no site functionality is affected.</li>
              <li>Whichever option is chosen, the choice is stored in browser local storage and the question is not asked again; clearing browser data causes the question to be asked again.</li>
              <li>After consent, the metrics measured include page views, sessions, average engagement time, bounce behaviour, and the ratio of new to returning visitors. IP anonymisation (<code>anonymize_ip</code>) is enabled on this site. Google Analytics uses IP addresses at collection time to provide the basic service and to determine approximate location, but does not record or store full IP addresses. The data is not used for advertising or cross-site targeting.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>3. Conditions on networks in mainland China</h3>
            <p>The Google Analytics script is served from <code>googletagmanager.com</code>, which may fail to load or load slowly on some networks in mainland China. In such cases no data is reported even where the visitor has consented; this results from network conditions rather than the conduct of this site. It is also why Cloudflare Web Analytics is retained: it is the channel through which visitors in mainland China can be reliably counted.</p>
            <h3>4. Changing the analytics choice</h3>
            <p>Clearing browser local storage, or using a private window, causes the question to be asked again. To withdraw a previous consent, remove the <code>analytics-consent</code> entry and reload the page, then select "Decline".</p>

            <h2 id="retention">7. How long data is kept</h2>
